\section{Treat compatibility as a release test}

If a new release changes the only available \texttt{step} implementation to an incompatible interface, do not silently keep its old label. Preserve the old interface behind an adapter if possible, or ship a new major SONAME alongside the old one. Compare dynamic export lists, and run real clients compiled against prior headers without rebuilding them. Rebuilding may make an incompatible change look harmless because the compiler immediately adapts the new clients.
